{"qid":"Q233","names":["Malta"],"title":"Malta","endonym":{"native":"Malta","lang":"mt"},"capsule":"Malta achieved independence from the United Kingdom on 21 September 1964, becoming a republic on 13 December 1974 and joining the European Union on 1 May 2004. The Maltese archipelago — comprising Malta, Gozo, Comino, and smaller islets — occupies a strategic position in the central Mediterranean that made it a contested prize across antiquity and the medieval period, serving as the seat of the Knights of St. John (1530–1798) and thereafter as a key British naval base. Malta adopted the euro in 2008. Its economy, once dependent on British defense spending, shifted to manufacturing, tourism, and financial services; the country has become notable for its online gaming sector and, more recently, as a digital-assets jurisdiction.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. Modern sovereign state; island boundaries are unambiguous and fully documented.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[{"label":"Britannica: Malta","url":"https://www.britannica.com/place/Malta"},{"label":"Wikipedia: Malta","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Malta"}],"britannica":"place/Malta","cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"Malta","rulers":[{"qid":"Q983140","name":"George Borg Olivier","start":1962,"end":1971,"image":"Statue Giorgio Borg Olivier Castille Square Valletta n2.jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Statue%20Giorgio%20Borg%20Olivier%20Castille%20Square%20Valletta%20n2.jpg?width=320","imageLicense":{"license":"CC BY 2.5","artist":"Marie-Lan Nguyen","attributionRequired":true},"nativeName":"Ġorġ Borg Olivier","nativeLang":"mt